				<header class="content-item__header">
					<h3 class="content-item__title"><a href="https://muddywatersresearch.com/research/2026/mw-sofi-borrowingsales-0330/" title="How SOFI’s Borrowing Money and Booking it as a Sale Enriched Management (SOFI US)" class="content-item__title-link">How SOFI’s Borrowing Money and Booking it as a Sale Enriched Management (SOFI US)</a></h3>
				</header>

				
									<p class="content-item__excerpt">Muddy Waters is short SOFI. SOFI's management appears to have booked a $312 million loan from JPMorgan as if it were a sale—inflating reported profits and their own bonuses while shareholders bear ~15% annual dilution. In our first report, we highlighted unrecorded borrowings of $312 million. SOFI h&hellip; <a class="content-item__more" href="https://muddywatersresearch.com/research/2026/mw-sofi-borrowingsales-0330/" title="How SOFI’s Borrowing Money and Booking it as a Sale Enriched Management (SOFI US)">more <i class="fa fa-angle-right"></i></a></p>
							</div>
		</div>
	</article><!-- #post-3032 -->
	<article id="post-3023" class="content-item post-3023 reports type-reports status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry company-114">
		<div class="content-item__wrapper">
							<a href="https://muddywatersresearch.com/research/2026/sofi-11-questions/" title="SOFI: Eleven Questions, Zero Answers (SOFI US)" class="content-item__image-wrapper">
